From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 18:47:13 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Hold the turn card at one height so a tap never moves the
 board

Selecting a piece grew the turn card by up to 90px as its guidance text and
the Deselect button appeared, then shrank it again on the next tap. On a
phone that pushed the reserve out from under the finger that had just tapped
it; on desktop the card shares a grid row with the opponent's reserve, so the
board itself dropped and came back on every click.

- The detail slot is reserved at three lines, the tallest live guidance
  wraps to at any width the card is laid out at, and is never display:none.
- Deselect sits beside the headline instead of adding a row.
- The phone layout had trimmed the page's bottom padding to 5px along with
  the top; the bottom gets 1rem back (the top stays trimmed for the board).
- The borderless phone card loses 3px of vertical padding each side so a
  390x844 screen still fits without scrolling.
- CACHE bumped v43 -> v44; DECISIONS.md records the invariant; shell.test.js
  guards it.

Measured in Chromium at 320, 360, 390, 740x360 and 1280 wide: board, player
rows and rail keep their coordinates through idle, board selection, reserve
selection and king placement.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
